    "result": "## Implementation Complete\n\nI've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval`. Here's what was done:\n\n### 1. **CLI Changes** (`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`)\n- Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option that can be specified multiple times\n- Created `parseThresholds()` function to validate threshold format and values\n- Updated `runEvalCommand()` to parse thresholds and pass them to `generateReport()`\n- Exit code handling: 0 when all pass, 1 when any fail, 2 on validation errors\n- Validation errors list valid metric IDs\n\n### 2. **Core Eval Module** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`)\n- Updated `generateReport()` to accept optional `thresholds` parameter\n- For each threshold:\n  - Metric with no score (null/undefined) fails the threshold\n  - Score >= min passes, otherwise fails\n- Report includes:\n  - `passed`: boolean indicating if all thresholds passed (true when no thresholds)\n  - `thresholds`: array with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` for each threshold\n\n### 3. **Report Formatting** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`)\n- Markdown reports gain \"## Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL for each\n- JSON reports automatically include the new fields via the updated report object\n\n### 4. **Documentation**\n- Updated both CLI and Core package READMEs with threshold option details\n- Added SDK example showing how to use thresholds programmatically\n\n### 5. **Backward Compatibility**\n- Without `--threshold`, behavior is identical to before\n- No new fields added to reports when thresholds not specified\n- All existing tests continue to pass\n\n### Threshold Validation\n- Format: `<metric>=<number>` (e.g., `exact_match=0.9`)\n- Valid metrics: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`\n- Valid range: 0 to 1 (inclusive)\n- Errors exit with code 2 and list valid metric IDs\n\nThe implementation works with both built-in metrics and custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations()`.",
